Prerequisites
=============
Install required Python modules:

  Ubuntu:
    apt-get install python-paramiko
    pip install pexpect

  RHEL:
    yum install python-paramiko.noarch
    pip install pexpect

  SLES:
    Install python-devel, python-setuptools
    Download pycrypto-2.6.1.tar.gz and paramiko-1.16.0.tar.gz
    python setup.py build && python setup.py install  (for pycrypto)
    easy_install ./  (for paramiko)
    pip install pexpect

Links:
  https://pypi.python.org/packages/source/p/pycrypto/pycrypto-2.6.1.tar.gz


Parameters (network_virtualization.yaml)
========================================
  hmc_username      HMC user name
  hmc_pwd           HMC password
  manageSystem      HMC managed system (CEC) name
  slot_num          Starting slot number (e.g., "20") or space-separated slot numbers
  vios_names        Space-separated VIOS names (one per backing device or shared)
  sriov_adapters    Space-separated SR-IOV adapter location codes (DRC)
  sriov_ports       Space-separated port numbers (e.g., "0 1" for round-robin)
  bandwidth         Bandwidth entitlement % per vNIC port
  priority          Space-separated failover priorities (1=highest, 100=lowest, 50=default)
  auto_failover     1 to enable, 0 to disable (default: 1)
  device_ip         Space-separated IPs to assign to each vNIC (or base IP)
  netmasks          Space-separated netmasks (one per vNIC or shared)
  peer_ip           Space-separated peer IPs used for ping validation
  peer_user         Peer LPAR login user
  peer_password     Peer LPAR login password
  mac_id            Space-separated MAC addresses (leave empty for HMC auto-generation)
  count             Number of failover/disable-enable iterations (default: 1)
  num_of_dlpar      Number of DLPAR remove+add iterations (default: 1)
  host_public_ip    Public IP of the test host (used to copy eeh_tool to VIOS)
  host_password     Test host login password
  user_name         Test host login user

  Extra Parameters for 6x Tests & Same-Port Tests:
  -----------------------------------------------
  device_ips        6 space-separated client IP addresses (fallback to device_ip)
  peer_ips          6 space-separated peer IP addresses (fallback to peer_ip)
  sriov_mac_id      MAC for direct SR-IOV logical port (test_sriov_vnic_same_port)
  sriov_device_ip   Client IP for direct SR-IOV port (test_sriov_vnic_same_port)
  sriov_peer_ip     Peer IP for direct SR-IOV port (test_sriov_vnic_same_port)


Execution Guide
===============
Always execute tests serially using:
  avocado run --max-parallel-tasks=1 <test_target> -m <yaml_file>

Master Config File:
  io/net/virt-net/network_virtualization.py.data/network_virtualization.yaml


Test Execution Commands
=======================

1. test_vnic_6x_single_card
   DLPAR add 6 vNIC interfaces backed by a single SR-IOV card.
   - Slot numbers: starts from starting slot (e.g. 20 -> 20,21,22,23,24,25)
   - Ports: round-robin across provided sriov_ports (e.g. "0 1")
   - MACs: auto-generated by HMC if mac_id is empty
   - IPs: uses device_ips and peer_ips (6 entries)
   Run:
     avocado run --max-parallel-tasks=1 \
       io/net/virt-net/network_virtualization.py:NetworkVirtualization.test_vnic_6x_single_card \
       -m io/net/virt-net/network_virtualization.py.data/network_virtualization.yaml

2. test_vnic_6x_multi_card
   DLPAR add 6 vNIC interfaces spread across multiple SR-IOV cards.
   - Requires >= 2 distinct cards in sriov_adapters; cancels otherwise
   - Round-robin across distinct cards and ports
   - MACs: auto-generated by HMC if mac_id is empty
   - IPs: uses device_ips and peer_ips (6 entries)
   Run:
     avocado run --max-parallel-tasks=1 \
       io/net/virt-net/network_virtualization.py:NetworkVirtualization.test_vnic_6x_multi_card \
       -m io/net/virt-net/network_virtualization.py.data/network_virtualization.yaml

3. test_sriov_vnic_same_port
   Add one direct SR-IOV logical port AND one vNIC backed by the same
   physical adapter and port. Verifies both simultaneously, then removes both.
   Run:
     avocado run --max-parallel-tasks=1 \
       io/net/virt-net/network_virtualization.py:NetworkVirtualization.test_sriov_vnic_same_port \
       -m io/net/virt-net/network_virtualization.py.data/network_virtualization.yaml

4. test_add / test_remove
   Add or remove one or more vNIC interfaces via HMC.
   Run:
     avocado run --max-parallel-tasks=1 \
       io/net/virt-net/network_virtualization.py:NetworkVirtualization.test_add \
       -m io/net/virt-net/network_virtualization.py.data/network_virtualization.yaml

5. test_backingdevadd / test_backingdevremove
   Add or remove secondary backing devices on an existing vNIC.
   Requires the vNIC to already be present (run test_add first).
   Run:
     avocado run --max-parallel-tasks=1 \
       io/net/virt-net/network_virtualization.py:NetworkVirtualization.test_backingdevadd \
       -m io/net/virt-net/network_virtualization.py.data/network_virtualization.yaml

6. test_disable_enable_dev
   Disable and re-enable a vNIC via HMC, verify link and ping survive.
   Run:
     avocado run --max-parallel-tasks=1 \
       io/net/virt-net/network_virtualization.py:NetworkVirtualization.test_disable_enable_dev \
       -m io/net/virt-net/network_virtualization.py.data/network_virtualization.yaml

7. test_hmcfailover
   Trigger HMC-initiated failover between backing devices, verify
   active device changes and connectivity is maintained.
   Run:
     avocado run --max-parallel-tasks=1 \
       io/net/virt-net/network_virtualization.py:NetworkVirtualization.test_hmcfailover \
       -m io/net/virt-net/network_virtualization.py.data/network_virtualization.yaml

8. test_clientfailover
   Trigger guest-initiated failover by writing to
   /sys/devices/vio/<id>/failover, verify connectivity after each flip.
   Run:
     avocado run --max-parallel-tasks=1 \
       io/net/virt-net/network_virtualization.py:NetworkVirtualization.test_clientfailover \
       -m io/net/virt-net/network_virtualization.py.data/network_virtualization.yaml

9. test_vnic_auto_failover
   Swap priorities of active and backing devices, verify the backing
   device with priority=1 becomes active automatically.
   Run:
     avocado run --max-parallel-tasks=1 \
       io/net/virt-net/network_virtualization.py:NetworkVirtualization.test_vnic_auto_failover \
       -m io/net/virt-net/network_virtualization.py.data/network_virtualization.yaml

10. test_rmdev_viosfailover
    Remove the VIOS vNIC server and backing device via rmdev/mkdev on
    the VIOS, verify failover to peer VIOS and connectivity recovery.
    Run:
      avocado run --max-parallel-tasks=1 \
        io/net/virt-net/network_virtualization.py:NetworkVirtualization.test_rmdev_viosfailover \
        -m io/net/virt-net/network_virtualization.py.data/network_virtualization.yaml

11. test_vnic_dlpar / test_vnic_hmc_dlpar
    Hot-remove and hot-add the vNIC via OS drmgr or HMC chhwres.
    Run:
      avocado run --max-parallel-tasks=1 \
        io/net/virt-net/network_virtualization.py:NetworkVirtualization.test_vnic_dlpar \
        -m io/net/virt-net/network_virtualization.py.data/network_virtualization.yaml

12. test_vnic_eeh
    Inject an EEH error on the backing device from VIOS using
    eeh_tool_64, verify failover and connectivity recovery.
    Run:
      avocado run --max-parallel-tasks=1 \
        io/net/virt-net/network_virtualization.py:NetworkVirtualization.test_vnic_eeh \
        -m io/net/virt-net/network_virtualization.py.data/network_virtualization.yaml

13. Run Entire Test Class
    Run:
      avocado run --max-parallel-tasks=1 \
        io/net/virt-net/network_virtualization.py:NetworkVirtualization \
        -m io/net/virt-net/network_virtualization.py.data/network_virtualization.yaml
